<title>USA: Unisys chairman/CEO to resign - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Unisys chairman/CEO to resign - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unisys Corp Chairman and Chief Executive James Unruh is expected to resign from the computer maker, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Thursday's electronic edition, the Journal said a successor has not yet been found, but that an announcement was expected to be made about his departure later today.</p>
<p>Unnamed industry executives told the Journal that the company has hired a firm to find a successor, but that his resignation may not take effect for several months.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
